    "reading": {
        "body": "Lambda's API was healthy for only 38.6 percent of observations in this window, making it an outlier that pulls the provider average down sharply and signals a reliability problem no other provider in this dataset comes close to matching.\n\nOf the twelve providers tracked since August 14, 2026, five recorded a perfect 100 percent healthy rate across roughly 107 observations each: AssemblyAI, Cohere, Deepgram, Groq, and Stability AI. Most of the remaining providers cluster between 97 and 99 percent. OpenAI is the second-weakest entry at 87.9 percent, a gap wide enough to matter for production workloads but still far above Lambda's figure. Lambda also has a slightly lower observation count at 101, which may reflect periods when the endpoint was unreachable rather than merely unhealthy, though the data does not say so explicitly.\n\nFor AI infrastructure, API uptime is the surface expression of what happens below it: compute availability, power continuity, and the operational stability of the facilities running inference. A provider at 38.6 percent healthy is not delivering a usable service regardless of the underlying model quality. The data covers less than three weeks and twelve providers, so it cannot speak to longer-term trends, root causes, or the full market. It also does not distinguish between partial degradation and complete outages, or between different endpoints within a single provider's offering.",
